> what is the range of x squared for a signed byte x
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x^2
  ucas: range it
range of it -> i8:
  -127..121   (44 distinct values)
  values: -127, -124, -119, -112..-111, -103, -95, -92, -87, -79, -71, -63, -60, -55, -47, -39, -31, -28, -23, -15, -7, 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, ...
  fits in i8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> funcs
it(x: i8) = x^2
  -> i8
> what is x squared
  ucas: it(x) = x^2
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = x^2
  -> real
> funcs
it(x: real) = x^2
  -> real
> is x squared even?
  note: "even": read as an even function, f(-x) = f(x), not an even number for every input (say "an even function" or "always even")
  ucas: it(x) = x^2
  ucas: parity it
parity of it:
  even: f(-x) = f(x)
  proved symbolically (parity rules: x is odd; sums keep a common parity, products multiply it; sin/tan/atan preserve it, cos/abs make it even)
> funcs
it(x: real) = x^2
  -> real
